{"root":"pli/ms","translators":["sujato"],"title":"Essentials","html":"<article id='an4.150'><header><ul><li class='division'><span class='root'>Aṅguttara Nikāya 4.150 </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Numbered Discourses 4.150 </span></li>\n<li><span class='root'>15. Ābhāvagga </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>15. Brightness </span></li></ul>\n<h1 class='sutta-title'><span class='root'>Sārasutta </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Essentials </span></h1></header>\n<p><span class='root'>“Cattārome, bhikkhave, sārā. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>“Mendicants, there are these four essentials. </span>\n<span class='root'>Katame cattāro? </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>What four? </span>\n<span class='root'>Sīlasāro, samādhisāro, paññāsāro, vimuttisāro—</span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>Ethics, immersion, wisdom, and freedom are essentials. </span>\n<span class='root'>Ime kho, bhikkhave, cattāro sārā”ti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'>These are the four essentials.” </span></p>\n<p class='endsutta'><span class='root'>Dasamaṁ. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='endvagga'><span class='root'>Ābhāvaggo pañcamo. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<p class='uddana-intro'><span class='root'>Tassuddānaṁ </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p>\n<blockquote class='uddanagatha'><p><span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Ābhā pabhā ca ālokā, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>obhāsā ceva pajjotā; </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>Dve kālā caritā dve ca, </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span>\n<span class='verse-line'><span class='root'>honti sārena te dasāti. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></span></p></blockquote>\n<p class='endbook'><span class='root'>Tatiyo paṇṇāsako samatto. </span><span class='translation' data-translator='sujato'></span></p></article>"}
